#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128983 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "5110af12-1d0a-5f7e-8a3b-626cc437c53e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6097" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128984 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "bd93891e-1f9f-51af-a5c2-4eb5ca1178d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6098" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "e51c2aa9-027b-5b23-bcaf-805804a8de9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6099" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\nI. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7897133d-d02c-5945-8bae-8de910dd401a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380805} {:answer/id #uuid "54db89e5-e388-5990-9e96-6d33b00ccfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380806} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4c5de8-a73c-5cb8-9dd9-0c297a741324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380807} {:answer/id #uuid "04a59ad9-9677-5f37-9301-07c3aa76d863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380808} {:answer/id #uuid "51d9985c-a105-5709-a583-8514b0a58599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a59ad9-9677-5f37-9301-07c3aa76d863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380808} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f205de5-26ea-5ee5-8cb4-b1e09776e3da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "738cc36c-dd11-5fb5-9dc6-f934d093f3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-129546" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812b461a-180e-543d-b8c3-60aec2c44810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442454} {:answer/id #uuid "99e7e82f-77a2-5e4c-b50f-29924bf0f0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442456} {:answer/id #uuid "9c03be65-b878-58d4-b8c0-c80d0b51e294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442459} {:answer/id #uuid "bece9adc-021f-5779-a2a6-dc4757a9f75c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442465} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b8ce6c-3373-5ebe-bc16-7d2a05cfc3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bece9adc-021f-5779-a2a6-dc4757a9f75c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442465} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c915c1b-8d9a-5d22-96f6-4f765b2be4a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "537e39b9-c554-5e1b-a6dd-8e198218680c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129548" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{y{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{y{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}[\\operatorname{tan}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cfce336-fbf4-557e-8201-f3dbb00f8284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442449} {:answer/id #uuid "555208da-41d1-5e38-a07f-d469aa40cdc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442450} {:answer/id #uuid "9bcf86e3-bcff-5511-b472-afb6bf1e0805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}+2{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442458} {:answer/id #uuid "a43bc8bc-5873-54d8-a5a8-9571bae2c78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442460} {:answer/id #uuid "c587c36b-a821-5e25-ba21-ae0e3fae2e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43bc8bc-5873-54d8-a5a8-9571bae2c78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442460} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30a14d3-7c0e-5fdd-bd22-94759a75c19a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59328584-c57e-5239-919a-177255c910ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-37925" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{e}^{x+y}]_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}({e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1})\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-{e}^{3}-({e}^{3}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbca2cc0-6c50-5ef1-b364-4c8340539f50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127214} {:answer/id #uuid "d4058351-2b5a-5891-947a-63bcf22087d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127215} {:answer/id #uuid "d4676da4-4594-50af-ba95-ac1bd8703441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127216} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4f67e6-6616-51fc-86a3-8c07ab6466fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127217} {:answer/id #uuid "01b6a70b-afbe-5f6e-9652-b8abf2d119f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b6a70b-afbe-5f6e-9652-b8abf2d119f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127218} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b13984-d467-5c08-a85b-7b772222d73c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6838355e-e160-5b83-9605-f7f195582fd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-37956" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}A$, where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}(\\frac{2}{5}(1)^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{5}(0)^{5/2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[\\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}((4)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "324de9dd-38ea-5337-bbde-d854373f1914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442445} {:answer/id #uuid "371c3423-1157-51d6-97e6-966f489c5487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442447} {:answer/id #uuid "714a7070-159e-549a-85fe-1667dab928ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442453} {:answer/id #uuid "a986dfcc-797e-520c-8aef-ae24d77f71bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442461} {:answer/id #uuid "c2466043-9164-57ad-b3f9-ec4567efd6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371c3423-1157-51d6-97e6-966f489c5487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442447} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0a1bbcd-9f99-5ffd-9c62-c5d07cca7e90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec2c5b36-cc64-59b6-941f-e3ef54e2e8b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72136" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27ca5ad7-f8d3-561b-9a26-e9c7eb4baa19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442444} {:answer/id #uuid "32c82e63-0ba1-5dd4-b1eb-9bb571d4a5f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442446} {:answer/id #uuid "6abefa77-d86f-5a30-92a1-7b7ba370ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442451} {:answer/id #uuid "b71f756d-5060-5655-9f9f-db68c84af53f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442464} {:answer/id #uuid "f099cea2-4241-50d0-b9de-7635c48e95d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f099cea2-4241-50d0-b9de-7635c48e95d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442469} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f52b29-b1dd-578a-b67a-9de7263fc4ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5334bf5b-4c65-5a0d-a9f7-2b79a628b6c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72176" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{4}\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1/4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1/4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:    \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\frac{1}{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $0$ to $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can also swap the order of integration. This gives \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}xy\\sqrt{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036213a9-48fc-584f-8639-59a3ce125042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336062} {:answer/id #uuid "1d527d5c-937e-5de5-994b-e3a247a82fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336304} {:answer/id #uuid "43ffcc44-4b70-5b78-8d03-2675f43c9d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336669} {:answer/id #uuid "6eea90aa-e74b-545d-b790-534b57b3fee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337015} {:answer/id #uuid "8acadba8-a72c-53d0-bdf7-778a4f0fb429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d527d5c-937e-5de5-994b-e3a247a82fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336304} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f04fafe-bb42-5814-ab3c-8eb7bec77bf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36d7ae2a-d2a1-510f-b695-22069db87971" :question/math-academy-id "q-72264" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{e}^{xy}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{1\\cdot y}-{e}^{0\\cdot y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y}-y]_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =({e}^{4}-4)-({e}^{0}-0)\\text{ } \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-4-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "334017b1-e361-54a4-8bd7-ca3fddb53769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382244} {:answer/id #uuid "b283798d-d944-5382-a5ed-61178e89abfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382245} {:answer/id #uuid "18a8f39a-f185-50c2-9632-4d71fb32f621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382246} {:answer/id #uuid "8febf0a3-ae0e-5e0b-ac73-ff0a95aeecb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382247} {:answer/id #uuid "323026fa-38e0-54a0-a86c-1691c6406fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18a8f39a-f185-50c2-9632-4d71fb32f621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382246} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef6b8e71-5f3a-569e-b59b-a38b1bed9ae6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d63f493d-43c5-52a2-9f1e-5afe59523cca" :question/math-academy-id "q-72266" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:        \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[16{y}^{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =16({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c8f36a-92b6-5bb7-be19-e00b34b2764a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}+e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336057} {:answer/id #uuid "20799050-832b-51da-8998-d217a55ed21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}+e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336337} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3c4583-5b56-5d2e-924c-b80ec83f8e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}-e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337142} {:answer/id #uuid "8b011d07-2efa-5d3a-9f67-aa59f09f5746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337289} {:answer/id #uuid "de6a90fe-27b5-54fb-9686-695f1dc16875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b011d07-2efa-5d3a-9f67-aa59f09f5746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337289} :answer-field/id #uuid "a054bb90-965c-5e55-9c44-54113e00e37e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37c838cf-74a0-548b-a26d-26e2da2f3576" :question/math-academy-id "q-72267" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{e}^{x+y}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{0+y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(e{e}^{y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y & =(e-1)[{e}^{y}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c72710f-c2e6-5f98-9934-8c0e10db39f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442441} {:answer/id #uuid "406a5e50-f9e7-5e1a-b74c-548956a80fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}({e}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442448} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8dbd40-65b4-55c4-825d-2641cb8d37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442457} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5cce45-dc22-5511-8d13-472d6c0e63cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}({e}^{2}-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442462} {:answer/id #uuid "e54da0da-f5e4-504a-8ffb-b66a2d635d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}({e}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54da0da-f5e4-504a-8ffb-b66a2d635d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}({e}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442468} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbeb3358-f2ea-5a4a-8dce-c539f418c1e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c3b5fdf-e81f-5835-8ccd-060ca0cabad4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73556" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}3y{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}3y{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y[{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y{[\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}]}_{0}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3}{4}y({e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3}{4}y({e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1){\\int }_{2}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1)\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1)(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27e36dff-223f-5b4e-b1b4-209444ae4750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339475} {:answer/id #uuid "295c3085-d512-5a69-92dc-71d06b0bdf20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339493} {:answer/id #uuid "83e36855-c02f-53e9-947d-e5e2682c194d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340315} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3f0e3a-443b-558d-9213-98e89a32d936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340527} {:answer/id #uuid "daea0c65-3b56-5a21-bd69-1ef30a29e1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27e36dff-223f-5b4e-b1b4-209444ae4750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339475} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0dec351-1e40-54db-9221-0fdc8d5c0c71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f9ea65f-55fc-5861-a64a-a45dd398be77" :question/math-academy-id "q-73578" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}(-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8087da-0be9-5661-8053-ef364f6d08fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442442} {:answer/id #uuid "258eca96-5244-5ca3-b0df-8541f47f4e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442443} {:answer/id #uuid "6d559819-b00a-5b69-960c-d3f8320ab0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442452} {:answer/id #uuid "87b99526-1110-5b37-a9b1-d2cd1aa88253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442455} {:answer/id #uuid "b2329388-28ae-5d8d-9a05-1bffa3cfe3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8087da-0be9-5661-8053-ef364f6d08fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442442} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b03b87-7f60-5a41-9452-146569702c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a0ea10f-00cc-5f1e-9234-e05424315508" :question/math-academy-id "q-73595" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{12}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{12}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{2}^{3}}+\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c0dc97-1bfa-5226-9e8a-83188a4da218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339328} {:answer/id #uuid "3785646e-da4d-5ce4-884b-7241e989b715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339627} {:answer/id #uuid "6b813e4f-15f3-5ca2-a873-e38985156d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340080} {:answer/id #uuid "7c522d09-2793-56be-8f5f-51c906dc7f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340247} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce6c823-b30e-5a3f-ac0b-98f3964eefdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c522d09-2793-56be-8f5f-51c906dc7f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340247} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc74d58b-4531-5b1b-ba07-fd90641c83fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69cbca99-1555-5b49-9e0d-f5bfd292b88d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73601" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(3+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{{3}^{1}-{3}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
